# Sync schedule → website + map

Whenever the trip schedule / itinerary changes in this project, **always update the interactive website** so days, places, timelines, and the journey map stay accurate.

## Project layout

- Website (GitHub Pages source): `docs/`
- Build scripts: `scripts/build_data.py`, `scripts/build_cafes.py`
- Family Excel (inspiration only): `reference/`
- Hebrew UI overlay: `docs/js/he-data.js` (site is Hebrew-first)

## Source of truth

- Collaborative planning draft: shared Google Sheet (`collab/config.json`, `source: "sheets"`) — check/sync first via `google-sheets-collab-sync` rule
- Structured builder: `scripts/build_data.py`
- Generated runtime data: `docs/js/data.js` (do not hand-edit unless necessary)
- Hebrew copy: `docs/js/he-data.js`
- Site UI: `docs/index.html`, `docs/js/app.js`, `docs/js/journey-map.js`, `docs/css/`

## Required workflow after any schedule change

1. Prefer reading the Google Sheet (`python3 scripts/fetch_collab_sheets.py`) when collab planning changed; then update `scripts/build_data.py` so `PLACES`, `DAYS` (dates, cities, titles, summaries, `placeIds`, `timeline`, transfers, hotels) match the new plan.
2. Regenerate data: `python3 scripts/build_data.py`
3. Update Hebrew strings in `docs/js/he-data.js` when titles/summaries/timeline notes change.
4. Confirm each day has distinct highlight places with `lat`/`lng` so the Maps journey markers do not stack on the hotel.
5. If the user wants the live site updated (or says “update the website” / “deploy”), commit the `docs/` changes and push `main` so GitHub Pages redeploys.
6. Briefly tell the user what itinerary days/places changed on the site/map.

## Do not forget

- Changing only notes under `reference/` is **not enough** — the website reads `docs/js/data.js` (+ Hebrew overlay).
- The journey map plots from day timelines/places; hotel-only points cause overlapping markers — prefer unique attractions per day.
- Keep booking checklist (`docs/js/checklist.js`) aligned if bookings/tickets change with the schedule.
